{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"REOPENED — this ticket's landed change (6125c534) was REVERTED via Gerrit 2616 (owned by incident ticket 90c7-c465-4037-42d5).\n\nWhat went wrong: 6125c534 merged on a VACUOUS Verified vote. The Verified workflow runs from trusted main via workflow_dispatch, so the newly-added required scanner-integration job never executed on the very change that introduced it — its native-scanner contracts (pytest SCANNER_INTEGRATION_NODES) were never actually run in CI. Once downstream changes did run it (after the dash `set -euo pipefail` portability bug was fixed in 6b034b9f8224), the contract step failed on every change, turning scanner-integration into a red required gate that blocked ALL merges.\n\nRedo guidance when this is picked up again: do NOT re-add a required scanner job until the vacuous-vote escape is closed (tracked in b973 / clubbable-teriyaki-oriole) — a newly-added required CI job must be proven to execute on its own introducing change, and its contracts must pass in CI, before its Verified vote can be trusted. Linking blocked_by b973."},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1788506614556578592,"uuid":"846a7ff4-23e8-4e26-81e2-6c016827fb47"}